-c, --count              Prefix each group with its count (minimum width 7).
-d, --repeated           First record of each repeated group.
-D, --all-repeated[=METHOD]   All repeated records (none, prepend, separate).
--group[=METHOD]         All records (separate, prepend, append, both).
-u, --unique             Singletons only.
-i, --ignore-case        Compare ignoring ASCII case; retain original spelling.
-f N, --skip-fields=N    Skip N fields, including leading blanks.
-s N, --skip-chars=N     Skip N characters after fields.
-w N, --check-chars=N    Compare at most N remaining characters.
-z, --zero-terminated    Use NUL for records and group separators.
--help, --version        Display documentation or the component version.
-- ends option parsing. Use - for stdin or stdout. A named output must be free.
Methods with long options require '='. -D defaults to none; --group defaults to separate.
none omits separators; separate inserts one between selected groups.
prepend inserts one before every group, append after every group, both at each boundary including the ends.
In C, -s and -w count bytes. In UTF-8 they count characters, treating each invalid byte as one character.
Count conflicts with -D. Group conflicts with -c, -d, -D and -u.
Without options, keep the first record in each adjacent run. Status 0 on success;
host errors return 1. NovaOS reports native argument, capability and I/O status.
